[{:seon.task/name "a-task-is-specified-once-a-proof-was-red"
  :seon.task/plan "A task's specification is its first proof (docs/plan.md Stage 1.2; the owner, 2026-11-14; root approved this design the same day). Evidence: 325 of 472 held backlog tasks with proofs have none written; random round 1's agent b6f1354dcc191912 spent turns 6-18 on a plan naming an uptime the page does not show, never wrote the proof its box scaffolded, and died at turn 19. Specified means: one of the task's proofs is written on its branch and has been red there since the branch's merge base, so it asserts something the code did not yet do (principles 3, a proof seen red first, enforced by a read that exists). `seon.ctx.status/status` answers it from `d/history` of `:seon.test/status` on each proof's var since `:seon.agent/base-commit`'s t, one seek a proof (1-3 a task). A proof green at its first verdict specifies nothing; the done rule's :no-change already refuses ending on it, and this says so before the work. `seon.render.ui/status-hiccup` opens its box list, while unspecified, with: your task isn't specified yet; its first proof is the specification: write it where it goes, run (prove), and see it red for the reason the plan gives; if the plan does not match the code you read, fix the plan first, (swap! ctx assoc-in [:seon.agent/task :seon.task/plan] ...). The line goes once a proof was red, one named edit. No reason is added to the done rule: specifying is a step, not a merge need, and the boxes stay the judge's reasons alone. Nothing gates the agent. A plan the agent improves is on its branch and merges to main by the one three-way merge (seon.merge, data's, once seon.task/carry-tx is gone: coordinate with data, never build on carry-tx), and reaches its task file after a Claude session reviews it (seon.source/a-task-files-entry-is-rewritten-in-place). Estimate: one history seek a proof each status, O(verdicts since the base); the render unchanged in order."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx.status-test/a-task-is-specified-once-a-proof-was-red seon.render-test/an-unspecified-task-is-told-specifying-is-first}}]
